# The OpenBot images the server, worker, migrations, computer and supervisor run from.
#
# Every way of running OpenBot from this checkout pulls them by this one tag:
#
#   ghcr.io/copilotkit/openbot-server, openbot-agent-computer and openbot-supervisor (Compose), and
#   ghcr.io/copilotkit/openbot, the all-in-one image (the release's image list).
#
# Read by scripts/start.sh, the end-to-end run (e2e/), CI, the release and internal-build workflows
# and Desktop's local build (desktop/scripts/local-build.sh), each of which hands it to Compose as
# OPENBOT_BACKEND_TAG. An OPENBOT_BACKEND_TAG in the environment or in .env wins over this line, to
# run another build. Running Compose by hand, pass this file first and .env after it, so .env still
# wins:
#
#   docker compose --env-file backend-images.env --env-file .env up -d
#
# A `sha-<commit>` tag names one build and never moves. Change it only to a build that was tested
# with this tree.
OPENBOT_BACKEND_TAG=sha-673965ebb4fdb22dcee3bf0100c30a01022f0f82
